title: Window3B
---
// Talk target of the window in 3B (Hotspots layer). At the viewing it is one of the three
// things he looks at; the first of them sets $r1_viewing_why, which moving day reads.
-> Look
    <<if $chapter == "R1Viewing" and $gate_r1_view_knock and not $gate_r1_view_window>>
        <<set $gate_r1_view_window to true>>
        <<done R1Viewing window>>
        <<face Samantha Player>>
        // PLACEHOLDER lines, from the old tour.
        <<if $r1_viewing_why == "">>
            <<set $r1_viewing_why to "light">>
            {$samantha_name}: Straight to the window. The part I always save for last.
        <<endif>>
        {$samantha_name}: Tram stop on the corner. Bakery opens at six. You'll hate it for a week, then you'll love it.
        {$samantha_name}: It opens if you ask it nicely. The last tenant never asked nicely.
        <<if $gate_r1_view_window and $gate_r1_view_kitchen and $gate_r1_view_bath>>
            <<note r1_view "Tell Samantha you've seen enough.">>
        <<endif>>
    <<elseif $chapter == "R1Viewing">>
        You: The tram stop, the bakery. Still there.
    <<else>>
        You: My window. Tram stop, bakery. She was right about the week.
    <<endif>>
===
